`GetType` was already only a few instructions, so any speedup will be small. This version copies `type` and `profile` into locals and adds a branch hint that the fast path (an explicit `type` is set) is the common case. Behavior is unchanged.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    const FIT_UINT8 t = type;
    if (__builtin_expect(t != FIT_UINT8_INVALID, 1))
        return t;

    const Profile::MESSAGE_FIELD_DEF_ENTRY_PLACEHOLDER_UNUSED_DUMMY *dummy = nullptr;
    (void)dummy;
    return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;
}
```

That draft guesses at type names, which is unsafe. Here is the corrected version, using `auto` so no type names need guessing:

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    const FIT_UINT8 t = type;
    if (__builtin_expect(t != FIT_UINT8_INVALID, 1))
        return t;

    const auto *p = profile;
    if ((p == NULL) || (profileIndex >= p->numFields))
        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;

    return p->fields[profileIndex].type;
}
```